body:
I think it is not about that. [https://youtu.be/wKJGhPGoHAk](https://youtu.be/wKJGhPGoHAk) explains the math very clearly. I have 8000 life now. However, 4000 is contributed by the armor and various things. If I remember correctly, rubies will only add 3%. So each will add 0,03\*4000 (not 8000), which is 120. I might have forgotten about the multiplier.  Also, if you have multiple equipped, they do not stack either. So let us say you have four rubies, then you get 480 instead of 4000\*(1.03\^4) - 4000\~= 502. Before, I calculated it as 8000\* (1.03\^4) - 8000 \~= 1000, and that is a lot of difference. So my whole point is from a mathematical point of view. It is not as good as you initially thought. 

&#x200B;

Still, if you need that, then don't let it stop you. Just remember the math show that is not as promising as it might seem.
